# Observability: the live view of a run, and nothing a run depends on.
#
# Kept apart from versions.env on purpose. That file pins what every benchmark
# cell must share, and nothing here is part of any cell: Prometheus and Grafana
# can be upgraded, moved or stopped between two cells of one sweep and neither
# cell changes. A setting that could change a cell does not belong in this file.
#
# Read by ops/prometheus.sh on the fleet host and ops/dashboards.sh on the
# workstation, so both ends of the tunnel agree on its port.

# The fleet host, as ssh knows it. Empty means Prometheus runs on this machine
# and no tunnel is opened, which is how the stack is smoke-tested against fake
# replicas. `-` rather than `:-`, so an explicitly empty GPU_HOST stays empty.
GPU_HOST="${GPU_HOST-nlp}"

# Prometheus, on the fleet host, loopback only.
#
# 9090 is another user's Prometheus, and 9091 — the port idea.md first planned
# for this one — had been taken by a third user's process by 2026-09-10. 19091
# sits below the kernel's ephemeral range (32768 and up), so no outbound
# connection is ever handed it by accident. ops/prometheus.sh still refuses to
# start if anyone holds it, because on a shared box a port is only free until
# somebody takes it.
PROMETHEUS_PORT="${PROMETHEUS_PORT:-19091}"

# Pinned together with the checksum of each archive it runs from. A platform
# with no checksum here is refused rather than fetched unchecked.
PROMETHEUS_VERSION="3.14.0"
PROMETHEUS_SHA256_linux_amd64="f665c6da19eb7ba399c915d30c7d9793c9b417bf8a749b504bc470678631478d"
PROMETHEUS_SHA256_darwin_arm64="a9623f7f4fe65b1b171b423c1a72bbf23dfdf41a171dcb33e7dd302af80dc01c"

# Where the release is unpacked. Outside the repository, so `make clean` does
# not throw the download away and nothing downloaded can be committed.
PROMETHEUS_HOME="${PROMETHEUS_HOME:-$HOME/.cache/kvroute}"

# How often every target is scraped.
#
# Five seconds is resolution enough to watch a 150 s cell move. Against the
# replicas it is one /metrics request each every five seconds, on engines the
# router itself reads every quarter second whenever the KV spill condition is
# on: noise beside that. The timeout sits under the interval, which Prometheus
# requires.
PROMETHEUS_SCRAPE_INTERVAL="5s"
PROMETHEUS_SCRAPE_TIMEOUT="4s"

# Bounded, because /home is shared. Whichever limit is reached first applies.
PROMETHEUS_RETENTION_TIME="7d"
PROMETHEUS_RETENTION_SIZE="2GB"

# The router's listen address, which is where Prometheus scrapes its /metrics.
# The sweeps start the router on 127.0.0.1:8080.
ROUTER_ADDR="${ROUTER_ADDR:-127.0.0.1:8080}"

# Grafana, on the workstation, in Docker, loopback only.
GRAFANA_VERSION="13.2.1"
GRAFANA_PORT="${GRAFANA_PORT:-3000}"
